                                                "sense_id": "2d8385b0-3baa-3aeb-a52b-382214a1535e",
                                                "text": "In essence, a furcula is a long, rigid stick, held underneath the body at high tension. When the springtail releases that pressure, the stick pushes down into the ground, or even the water's surface, like an upside-down medieval catapult, firing the springtail into the air in a semi-controlled manner."
                                            }
